sub1:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d-overall> .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Hannezo, Prost & Joanny (2014) PNAS & Krajnc & Ziherl (2015) PRE 3D epithelial sheet morphology (squamous-to-cuboidal-to-columnar scaling, apico-basal buckling & Gómez-Gálvez scutoid tube packing) — MorphoEval overall 82.4/100" ;
        dcterms:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dcterms:description "The remediation delivers what the script says it delivers: a genuine 3D polyhedral cell mesh on a curved tube (apical and basal periodic Voronoi tessellations of ~418 Hannezo-sized cells, scutoids detected as apical/basal neighbour-set mismatches, intercalations edge-balanced, Euler mean-6 verified on both surfaces, lateral-face area of the scutoid packing 0.87x the frustum packing at the WT crest), swept over surface ratio and coupled to every relaxed tissue through s_crest = 1 + h_0 kappa_max. It honestly labels itself a reduced model (no vertex energy, no T1 dynamics) and two new Lean theorems pin the isometric-limit and Euler identities. Re-scoring against the current code, however, lowers every dimension except where the new work adds: the 12-tissue aspect-ratio r = 1.0000 is circular (tensions back-solved from the observed ratios, no per-row provenance), the 'simulated' wavelength is 85 % the analytic prediction, the WT amplitude equals its reference by rescaling, the reference JSON's specimen block stores the script's own output, the continuum F[w] carries six uncited coefficients, the phase diagram is a threshold lookup with a hard-coded Gamma_b switch, and the fold-crest coupling over-predicts s_crest by 44 % with f_s saturated at ~1.0 for all six buckled/acinar tissues (no discriminating prediction). Overall 82.4 (model impl. 83.3, bio. val. 75.8, repro. 90.3), down from 93.4. Overall 82.4/100 (faithfulness 79.0, reproducibility 90.3); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 654cd6fc; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 82, Morphological realism / specimen match 78, Parameter expressivity 86, Morphometric validation 72, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 88, Reproducibility package 92. Output judged: docs/media/epithelial_buckling_3d_comparison.png: rendered output of 2016-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d.py at 654cd6fc, image/png, 1143971 B, 2876×1444 px, artifact_sha256 6269de61be241e71465e8aaa782e2860e0546a4d15b07d1fcaf6eceb76858a74 (sha256 6269de61be241e71465e8aaa782e2860e0546a4d15b07d1fcaf6eceb76858a74), spec_fingerprint c058d57a2503a59a583412118501c0ee7c1d08eac1445bb91a576986cd7b311b. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: c058d57a2503a59a583412118501c0ee7c1d08eac1445bb91a576986cd7b311b; artifact_sha256: 6269de61be241e71465e8aaa782e2860e0546a4d15b07d1fcaf6eceb76858a74; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/epithelial_buckling_3d/epithelial_buckling_3d_reference.json=eef9f75ed38ce872..., datasets/epithelial_buckling_3d/epithelial_sheet_buckling_specimen.jpg=cd05cc85a7f49dd2..., datasets/epithelial_buckling_3d/paper_citations.bib=77a77d7dc42170a5..., datasets/epithelial_buckling_3d/scout_manifest.json=99741cb299962b18..., datasets/epithelial_buckling_3d/scutoid_tube_reference.json=85d9db6cbb5b95ff...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-epithelial-buckling-3d-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Hannezo, Prost & Joanny (2014): single-cell energy E_cell(A) = (Gamma_a + Gamma_b) A + c Gamma_l V_0 / (2 sqrt A) gives h_0/d_0 = c Gamma_l / [4 (Gamma_a + Gamma_b)] spanning squamous/cuboidal/columnar; an elastic foundation selects lambda_c = 2 pi (kappa_eff / K_sub)^(1/4); apico-basal tension asymmetry sets a spontaneous curvature whose sign follows Gamma_a - Gamma_b | Krajnc & Ziherl (2015): convexity of the cell energy at equilibrium and the continuum elastic limit of the 3D vertex monolayer | Gómez-Gálvez et al. (2018): on curved tubes the basal/apical surface ratio makes Voronoi tessellations of the two surfaces differ; cells with apico-basal neighbour intercalations (scutoids) appear and their number increases with the surface ratio; reconstructed_in_script: Analytic + L-BFGS-B single-cell equilibrium (L205-271), quartic buckling wavelength (L274-287), a 5-regime threshold phase classifier (L289-317), a 2D pseudo-spectral Swift-Hohenberg-type relaxation F[w] with cubic (spontaneous-curvature) and quartic terms (L323-490), a 12-tissue table and 5 perturbations driven from epithelial_buckling_3d_reference.json (L863-1017), CV segmentation of one CC0 histology micrograph (L1023-1120), and (Pass 3) a doubly periodic Voronoi tube mesh with scutoid detection, surface-ratio sweep and fold-crest curvature coupling (L497-857); transfer_boundary: The 12-tissue Gamma_a/Gamma_b/Gamma_l/K_sub 'norm' values are not measured tensions; they reproduce aspect_ratio_obs through the Law-1 formula to <0.5 % per row and carry no per-row source, so the r = 1.0000 collapse is a parity check of the JSON with itself, not a test against the papers | lambda_sim = 0.85 lambda_c + 0.15 lambda_FFT (L467) and the WT amplitude is rescaled to fold_amplitude_ref_um (L454-455, L999), so the wavelength r = 0.9993 and the WT amplitude 'match' are dominated by construction | The scutoid mesh is a Voronoi projection (seeds fixed, lateral faces evaluated geometrically); it is not a relaxed 3D vertex model and no Gómez-Gálvez figure value is digitised - the scutoid reference values are geometric identities (f_s(1) = 0, mean neighbours 6, Spearman 1) plus a crest ratio derived from the already-pinned WT fold geometry; does_not_claim: A relaxed 3D vertex/scutoid energy (apical, basal and lateral tensions minimised with free vertices), T1 or apico-basal intercalation dynamics, quantitative agreement with the Gómez-Gálvez scutoid counts in salivary gland / egg chamber tubes, measured per-tissue surface tensions, or more than one histological specimen." ;
        dcterms:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 2016-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d.py:289-317 and 960-966 — the 5-regime phase diagram is a threshold lookup (K_sub <= 0.011, asym >= 0.28, 0.85 <= AR <= 2.40, K_sub <= 0.022) and the plotting loop injects the acinar asymmetry by switching Gamma_b from 0.75 to 0.40 whenever K_sub <= 0.011. Derive the flat / folded / acinar boundaries by comparing the relaxed energies energy_final of the three seeded states at each grid point (the relaxation already returns them, L395 / L487), and sweep Gamma_a - Gamma_b as a proper axis instead of the K_sub-gated switch.",
            "remediation needed: 2016-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d.py:401-408, 455 and 467 — the continuum F[w] coefficients 1.35, 0.85, 0.15, 1.65, 2.2 (anisotropy), 2.20 (BETA) and 1.48 are uncited. Either derive them from the Hannezo Eqs. (6)-(11) weak-nonlinear expansion (and state the derivation in the docstring) or label them as surrogate fitting constants in the header, the README and the KG yaml so the 'L-BFGS-B relaxed' panels are not read as first-principles predictions.",
            "remediation needed: 2016-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d.py:461-467 and 454-459 — lambda_sim = 0.85 lambda_c + 0.15 lambda_fft and the amplitude rescale to target_amplitude_um make the wavelength correlation (r = 0.9993, RMSE 11.15 um) and the WT amplitude (42.5 = 42.5 um) outputs of the inputs. Report lambda_fft alone as the emergent wavelength (the 64-point grid on a 3 lambda_c box quantises it; use a finer grid or Gaussian peak interpolation), drop the blend, and derive the amplitude from the supercritical balance sqrt(mu/BETA) scaled by h_0 instead of the reference value; then let the comparison fail or pass on its own.",
            "remediation needed: 2016-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d.py:582-662 — the scutoid mesh fixes the seeds and projects them radially; the lateral faces are trapezoid/triangle areas and nothing is minimised, so the mesh cannot respond to Gamma_l, Gamma_a or Gamma_b and the 'lateral area saving' 0.874 is a geometric fact about Voronoi projection, not an equilibrium. Implement the reduced 3D vertex step the Pass 3 header promises as the residual: relax the apical and basal seed positions (or vertex positions) under E = Gamma_a A_a + Gamma_b A_b + Gamma_l A_lat with the volume constraint, and show that the scutoid fraction at fixed s changes with Gamma_l / (Gamma_a + Gamma_b).",
            "remediation needed: 2016-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d.py:752-791 and 1811-1820 — s_crest from the 99th-percentile of the low-passed spectral curvature is 3.326 against the sinusoidal estimate 2.303 computed from the pinned WT fold geometry (44 % over), because the relaxed sheet's amplitude (50.4 um) and wavelength (115.6 um) differ from the reference 42.5 / 136.4 um; with f_s saturated at 1.0 for every buckled tissue the crest coupling has no discriminating power. Compute s_crest from the reference (A, lambda, h_0) triple per tissue as well as from the sheet, extend the sweep grid between s = 1 and 2.5 where f_s is still rising, and add a measurement comparing the predicted scutoid fraction with a published scutoid count (Gómez-Gálvez 2018 Fig. 2/3 salivary gland or egg chamber values, digitised and vendored with a figure pinpoint).",
            "remediation needed: datasets/epithelial_buckling_3d/epithelial_buckling_3d_reference.json:300-313 with 2016-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d.py:1760-1779 — the specimen_histology_reference block stores the script's own segmentation output (59.66 px, 13.31 px, 4.4833, 264.0 px, 4.4252) as the 'reference', while the measurements compare against 4.48 / 4.45 attributed to Hannezo / Štorgel without a locator. Replace the block with independently obtained values (manual annotation of the same micrograph by a second method, or a Štorgel 2016 table value with its table number) and pin the 4.48 / 4.45 references to a figure or table.",
            "remediation needed: datasets/epithelial_buckling_3d/epithelial_buckling_3d_reference.json:56-236 with 2016-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d.py:880-897 and 924-934 — the per-tissue Gamma_a/Gamma_b/Gamma_l 'norm' values reproduce aspect_ratio_obs through Law 1 to <0.5 % on every row and carry no source, so the 12-tissue aspect-ratio r = 1.0000 / RMSE 0.0041 / alpha = 0.994 is a parity check of the JSON with itself. Either (a) replace the tensions with independently reported values (e.g. Sui et al. 2018 laser-ablation recoil ratios for the wing disc; Krajnc/Štorgel columnar estimates) and report the resulting, imperfect, correlation, or (b) relabel the measurement as 'Law-1 parity' with reference_value 1.0 and remove it from the specimen-match evidence; add a per-row `source` field (paper, figure/table) to every tissue and perturbation row." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.824"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Claude Fable 5.1 (MorphoEval Autonomous Loop Slot 047 Pass 3 Assessor)" ;
        dcterms:identifier "claude-fable-5-1" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf orcid:0009-0007-4948-9192 ;
        foaf:homepage <https://www.anthropic.com> .
}

